cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  Please cite this software when using RAZOR. When using the calibration
  data, also cite RazorCal and retain applicable upstream attribution.
title: "RAZOR: Pruning Replaceable Experts in LLMs"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mingyang
    family-names: Song
    email: nickmysong@tencent.com
    affiliation: "Foundation Model Department, Tencent"
  - given-names: Mao
    family-names: Zheng
    affiliation: "Foundation Model Department, Tencent"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nick7nlp/Razor"
url: "https://github.com/nick7nlp/Razor"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30465"
    description: "arXiv:2609.30465 -- the preprint describing RAZOR"
  - type: url
    value: "https://huggingface.co/collections/Nickyang/razor"
    description: Hugging Face collection of the released pruned models
abstract: >
  RAZOR is a training-free expert pruning method for mixture-of-experts
  models. It scores functional replaceability with consensus residuals, using
  an exact single-deletion identity that accounts for survivor renormalization
  and router-selected refill, and aggregates the scores by conditional RMS over
  calibration tokens. The repository provides RAZOR, its RCS and RCS-LOO
  scoring variants, the REAP, EAN and frequency baselines, model adapters and
  the RazorCal calibration corpus.
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - model-compression
  - pruning
  - counterfactual-saliency
  - calibration-dataset
